+
+### Seeding
+
+After `npm install`, configuring `DATABASE_URL`, and applying migrations, run:
+
+```bash
+npm run db:seed
+```
+
+This inserts 15 starter item categories. Existing item codes and display names
+are preserved. Review the codes in `prisma/seed.ts` when defining the Jotform
+normalizer's mapping. It does not insert quantities, submissions, activities,
+or valuations by default.
+
+To populate all five models in a development/test database, run:
+
+```bash
+npm run db:seed:demo
+```
+
+Demo mode also creates two items with `DEMO_` codes, four opening counts for
+2026 (two items at each location), two fictional per-unit valuations, and four
+`SEED_DEMO_` source submissions containing eight IN/OUT activity rows. These
+are development fixtures, not actual Jotform records, physical counts, or
+approved IRS valuations. Use a development/test Neon branch for demo data.
+
+Both commands are safe to rerun sequentially: duplicates are skipped or found
+by unique keys, existing records are preserved, and existing submissions never
+receive another set of activities. All changes from a run occur in one
+transaction; a failed run rolls back its data changes. Seeding is explicit and
+does not run automatically on application startup or migration. Prisma loads
+the seed command from `prisma.config.ts` and executes it with `tsx`.
 
